# mkdir -- deps.list
#
# Wave: R50 -> v1.1-A extraction
# Doc:  paideia-os design/tooling/plan.md §7 (shared-library roster);
#       this repo's design/architecture.md (v1.1-A section).
#
# One row per shared-library dependency. `pkg install mkdir`
# resolves this list transitively at install time and refuses the
# install if any row's dual-sig verification fails.
#
# Row format (I3-consistent with libpdx-argv, libpdx-cap):
#   <name>@<semver> <ml-dsa-65-author-fp> <ml-dsa-65-paideia-root-fp>
#
# v1.1-A: no dependencies
# -----------------------
#
# v1.1-A is a single-file straight-line tool that inlines the three
# syscalls it needs (sys_mkdir=79, sys_debug_puts=12, sys_exit=60)
# and reads argv directly from the frozen execve ABI (rdi=argc,
# rsi=argv). This is the same one-file-one-ELF pattern that the
# paideia-os /bin/mkdir at `src/user/mkdir.pdx` uses today (and
# every sibling: true / cat / cp / mv / rm / touch).
#
# Retired from M5-era pins
# ------------------------
#
#   libpdx-argv              -- v1.1-A reads argv directly; no
#                                Parser::parse_argv call.
#   libpdx-cap               -- v1.1-A holds no caps at exec.
#   libpdx-audit             -- v1.1-A emits no audit records; the
#                                seam relands on libpdx-audit's real
#                                marshaller at v1.2-A.
#   libpdx-semantic-pipe     -- v1.1-A stages no CreatedDirRecord[];
#                                the emit relands together with the
#                                audit hookup at v1.2-A.
#
# Every one of the four M5-era pins is grep-verified NEVER linked in
# `src/` at any point in the M1..M5 scaffold either -- see
# `design/enhancement-plan.md` §3.7 for the audit that surfaced the
# three-of-four overstatement at the tail of milestone #6. libpdx-argv
# was the one actual link neighbour at M5; v1.1-A drops it.

# --- Real dependency set (grep-verified: none) ---

# (intentionally empty at v1.1-A)

# EOF
